

UPTIME(1)           UNIX Programmer's Manual              UPTIME(1)



NAME
     uptime - show how long the system has been running

SYNOPSIS
     uptime

DESCRIPTION
     _U_p_t_i_m_e prints the current time, how long the system has
     been up, and the number of users logged in.

     It is w(1) under another name: /bin/uptime and /bin/w are two
     directory entries for one inode, and the program chooses its
     behaviour from the name it was invoked by.  `w -u' prints the
     same line.

     Elapsed time is measured from the 60 Hz system tick counter,
     which counts from boot: about one second of precision, good
     to roughly two years.

FILES
     /etc/utmp     the login accounting file, for the user count

SEE ALSO
     w(1), who(1), ps(1)

BUGS
     No load average is printed, this system keeping no run-queue
     average.  See w(1) for the rest of what is not measured.

FGX                            2.11BSD                           1
